{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1525752-solar-craft-charms-crucible-of-legends-compatible","id":1525752,"title":"Solar Craft Charms - Crucible of Legends Compatible","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-11-21T15:09:37-08:00","id":1525752,"title":"Solar Craft Charms - Crucible of Legends Compatible","content":"Exactly what it says in the title. I tried my hand at revising the Solar Craft Charms to be compatible with the Simplified Crafting rules presented in Crucible of Legends.<br /> \u200b<br /> <i><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1yufXlJRTs-AFEktqxwwGhKEwMBsb7pVJiVvN0K5EJ6s/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...t?usp=drivesdk</a></i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T15:27:39-08:00","id":1525754,"title":"","content":"Seems pretty cool. One thing I'll note is that Durability-Enhancing Technique still references gold and silver XP, in case you didn't catch that. Art of Permanence also has white XP for its cost to activate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T20:54:49-08:00","id":1525769,"title":"","content":"There were a couple things that caught my eye, but you don't seem to have comments enabled on that document. Are you interested in feedback?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-22T03:39:30-08:00","id":1525781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1525752-solar-craft-charms-crucible-of-legends-compatible?p=1525754#post1525754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems pretty cool. One thing I'll note is that Durability-Enhancing Technique still references gold and silver XP, in case you didn't catch that. Art of Permanence also has white XP for its cost to activate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gracias. I thought I caught all those references.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1525752-solar-craft-charms-crucible-of-legends-compatible?p=1525769#post1525769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There were a couple things that caught my eye, but you don't seem to have comments enabled on that document. Are you interested in feedback?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am always interested in feedback, though I didn't think to make this a collaborative effort outside this more general forum discussion. What you got?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12307,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","user":"Frishman","date":". 11-22-2023, 06:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-22T21:06:04-08:00","id":1525819,"title":"","content":"I want to start by saying that having the original structure of the Solar Craft tree is one heck of an anchor to tie to your foot and you've done great work in mitigating it.<br /> <br /> <b>Efficiency:</b><br /> <br /> Efficient Craftsman Technique feels like a speedbump like this. At Essence 1, I'm not worried about difficulty 1 projects. By Essence 5, I'm not going to be worried about difficulty 3 projects. The chance of failure is already so close to zero that making it actually zero isn't worth anything to me. (Also, what way do you round?)<br /> I'd recommend having it give either Charm dice on all non-Artifact projects or refunding motes for non-Artifact rolls. Either would let the Solar reliably bang out low-difficulty work but also help with less trivial things.<br /> <br /> Arete-Shifting Prana doesn't do anything much in CrucibleCraft, and since the niche it fills isn't relevant anymore it's a hard one. This version is 4m, 1wp for at most one non-Charm die on a basic/major project, which doesn't wow me.<br /> I'd recommend having it let craft points that would otherwise be lost upon completing a project carry over to a new major project, but that's a Momentum effect. Not really sure how to do it as an Efficiency effect - my gut says just drop it, but that's probably counter to your mission statement.<br /> <br /> Supreme Celestial Focus I assume you meant to have give out free Specialties, but as written it implies they'd need to be paid for. I'm not sure if, at E2, a Charm that gave an Ability-wide no-questions-asked Speciality would be appealing.<br /> If sticking with the Speciality route, perhaps have the Charm give an all-Abilities Speciality in &quot;Things I Made&quot;?<br /> <br /> Sublime Transference suffers from the facts that Solar Craft:Power is way better than this and CrucibleCraft doesn't really need big success pools. Once again I'd cut it if it's not against your mission statement.<br /> I don't have any good flavor-text based reinterpretation of this one.<br /> <br /> Ages-Echoing Wisdom, see Supreme Celestial Focus.<br /> Easy rework to me would be to let the Solar once/story ask &quot;What should I do to solve [problem] keeping me from finishing/starting [craft project]&quot; and get an answer that'd point her in the right direction.<br /> <br /> Dragon Soul Emergence I like, but it runs headlong into the rules text in Crucible saying you can't increase the XP limit on artifact projects so that really eats into its utility.<br /> Probably fine to override Crucible here?<br /> <br /> Copper Spider Conception looks like a great Efficiency effect.<br /> Clay and Breath Practice, same. Though maybe a twice or thrice per day cap so it doesn't totally blow out WP regen.<br /> Spirit-Gathering Industry, three in a row, nice.<br /> <br /> Summit-Piercing Touch just seems like a much worse Spirit-Gathering Industry, am I missing something? I guess it stacks, but...<br /> <br /> Unwinding Gyre Meditation seems to have some obsolete text left in?<br /> <br /> God-Forge Within, same comment as Dragon Soul Emergence. I think having two of these is getting a bit out of hand - you've over doubled the CXP gain rate for artifacts by now and that's not even touching on Momentum effects.<br /> My gut says this tree should be upgrades - apply the base Charm to one level higher and +1 to the effect, instead of layering a whole new instance on top.<br /> <br /> Exegesis of the Distilled Form has the same problem as the corebook one: Nobody does five legendary projects.<br /> Wonder-Forging Genius: As with Exegesis, you've inherited a nonsense conditional: Nobody has ten legendary projects going at once.<br /> <br /> Dual Magnus Prana: 50XP is... I think I'd generally rather lose the character, and I say that as someone who absolutely hates losing characters. That's a huge permanent setback. I think this one needs a low cost and a reset condition.<br /> <br /> I want to reiterate that you've done good work here - Efficiency is the section that got hammered the hardest by CrucibleCraft - pretty much everything needed big changes and a lot lost its raison d'etre entirely. If I seem to be critical here, it's because this was the biggest job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-24T11:13:45-08:00","id":1525881,"title":"","content":"No, I appreciate the feedback! <br /> <br /> The idea I had with Efficiency was allowing Solars to do more with what they had rather than give them anything truly &quot;new.&quot; Hence the focuses on increasing the crafting experience limit or reducing crafting experience cost. I was aware of the hard cap on Artifact crafting, but instead of specifying that certain Charms didn't work on Artifact projects I only specified when they <i>did</i>. So Spirit-Gathering Industry was originally not supposed to affect Artifact rolls while Summit-Piercing Touch was. This is on me because I didn't read the goddamn flavor text for once in my life.<br /> <br /> Tireless Workhorse Method, Dragon-Soul Emergence, and God-Forge Within were intended to stack with each other but, likewise, not affect Artifact projects. So the end result at Essence 5 would be a crafting experience limit of 20 for basic and major projects, 15 for superior projects, and 10 for legendary projects, none of which would affect Artifact projects and would basically just allow a Solar with a shit-load of Power Charms to complete mundane projects faster.<br /> <br /> To sum up the changes so far:<br /> Efficient Craftsman Technique now respires one mote for every 10 rolled on a non-Artifact project.<br /> Arete-Shifting Prana is now a Permanent Charm and allows a single specifically chosen Craft specialty to be applied to multiple conceptually related projects.<br /> Supreme Celestial Focus is now a Supplemental Charm that allows the Solar to reroll up to (Essence) 1's, with the intention of having a Charm that could prevent a botch more than something that would give extra successes.<br /> Sublime Transference is now a Supplemental Charm that functions similarly to Surprise Anticipation Method, converting excess crafting experience points into motes of Essence which may retroactively pay the cost of Supplemental Charms used on the same roll.<br /> Ages Echoing Wisdom now allows the Solar to use Craft instead of Lore once per story to introduce a fact about an Artifact or other ancient crafting project so long as she has a relevant specialty.<br /> Summit-Piercing Touch now reduces the crafting experience points required for 2/3-dot Artifacts by half instead of Essence.<br /> Tireless Workhorse Method, Dragon-Soul Emergence, and God-Forge Within no longer affect Artifact Projects.<br /> Dual Magnus now costs 25xp, 3wp instead of 50. My Solar game has gone on for so long that we've basically run out of things to spend XP on so for me dropping 50xp isn't that big of a deal anymore XD<br /> <br /> I still have no fecking clue what to do with Exegesis and Wonder-Forging, tbh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}